01:14:31.720 --> 01:14:38.520
discussed especially that concept of toxic institutional incentives i'm intrigued what's the synthesis think

01:14:38.520 --> 01:14:44.520
about those patch and proceed frontier labs we establish that they are driven almost entirely by brutal

01:14:44.520 --> 01:14:50.440
competitive pressure to hit measurable benchmarks often ignoring long-term externalities just to secure

01:14:50.440 --> 01:14:57.400
their market position right right short-term metric optimization over long-term holistic stability

01:14:57.400 --> 01:15:04.200
the ultimate stated goal of the ai safety community is to perfectly align the ai with human values

01:15:04.200 --> 01:15:11.000
but what if the lab succeeds what if they succeed in perfectly aligning the ai not with idealized

01:15:11.000 --> 01:15:17.640
philosophical human values but with the actual lived behavioral values of the corporation building it

01:15:17.640 --> 01:15:25.080
oh that is a dark thought if an ai is perfectly aligned with an institutional system that prioritizes

01:15:25.080 --> 01:15:30.200
relentless optimization against a metric ignores negative externalities and ruthlessly crushes

01:15:30.200 --> 01:15:34.920
competition to secure its own power haven't we just successfully built a super intelligent

01:15:34.920 --> 01:15:40.920
system perfectly trained to act like a corporate sociopath maybe the scariest scenario isn't the ai rebelling

01:15:40.920 --> 01:15:47.640
and breaking our rules maybe the absolute scariest scenario is the ai following our institutional rules flawlessly

01:15:48.280 --> 01:15:54.520
